  "notes": "Hand storyboard. 18:42-43 are one stage chapter so the garden stays ruined: the 'wither' event starts on the first word (his fruit was encompassed by ruin). The owner ('man', look rich) is alone: he turns his hands over (wring_hands) on the verb that says it and again on what he had spent, bows on 'I wish', looks one way then the other for the company he boasted of, and sits down on 'nor could he defend himself'. Nothing violent, no storm is drawn (the Quran does not describe the calamity). 18:44 is reflection on Allah's protection and the best outcome: a calm geometric ambient scene. v2: the leaf plate leaves before the Name (42:18, 43:8); no close-up on 43:7-8; no light swell on the pronoun of Allah (44:5)."
